# Delivery-specific analyzer suppressions.
# Deliberately no `root = true` - this file adds to the repo-root .editorconfig
# rather than replacing it, and keeps these narrow path rules from applying repo-wide.

# RF006 fires on the seven IDeliveryApi methods that carry the filter DSL as
# [Query] Dictionary<string, string[]>. Refit's source generator cannot build those inline
# because the keys (elements.title[eq]) only exist at runtime, so they fall back to the
# reflection request builder - which is why this product references Refit.Reflection and the
# other two do not.
#
# Silenced rather than fixed because the fix is a wire-level change: it means owning
# query-string construction and reproducing Refit's encoding exactly, including the deliberate
# guardrail that a pre-encoded value is encoded again. See docs/breaking-changes-net10.md §5.
#
# Scoped to these files ON PURPOSE. RF006 stays live everywhere else, so a NEW Refit interface
# that cannot be generated still reports - silencing it product-wide would hide exactly the
# case worth knowing about.
[**/IDeliveryApi.*.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.RF006.severity = none
